{"timestamp":"00:17:46.163","source":"Browser","level":"LOG","message":"{\"discipline\":\"Doctor\",\"environment\":\"Workflow\",\"manual\":\"1. Title  \\nMoving Large Numbers of Files and Exploring a Folder in Visual Studio Code\\n\\n2. Purpose  \\nThis work instruction describes how to move a large number of files to a folder named “Documents” and how to explore a folder within Visual Studio Code. All steps and features are based strictly on the visible actions in the provided screenshots.\\n\\n3. Prerequisites  \\n- Access to a storage device labeled \\\"Julia 1TB\\\".\\n- Access to a folder or location called “Documents”.\\n- Visual Studio Code installed and open.\\n- A folder named \\\"AI USER GUIDE GENERATOR\\\" available for exploration in Visual Studio Code.\\n- The specific workflow or function for doctors is not shown or described in the screenshots and therefore cannot be determined.\\n\\n4. Procedure  \\n**A. Move Files to the 'Documents' Folder**\\n1. Ensure you are working within the environment where you have access to the device “Julia 1TB”.\\n2. A process labeled “Moving 164,345 files to ‘Documents’” will display a status bar showing transfer progress, elapsed file numbers, time remaining, and speed (e.g., “18 seconds left (45.8 MB/s)”).\\n3. Wait for the progress bar to complete.\\n4. The process can be canceled by clicking the visible ‘X’ (close) button on the status window.\\n    - It cannot be determined how to initiate the move or select files, as this is not shown.\\n\\n**B. Explore a Folder in Visual Studio Code**\\n1. In Visual Studio Code, verify that the Explorer pane (on the left) displays at least one folder (e.g., “AI USER GUIDE GENERATOR”).\\n2. The main area of Visual Studio Code will display the Welcome screen with options:\\n    - New File\\n    - Open File…\\n    - Open Folder…\\n    - Clone Git Repository…\\n    - Connect to…\\n    - Generate New Workspace…\\n3. To explore the “AI USER GUIDE GENERATOR” folder, ensure it is expanded in the Explorer pane.\\n    - It cannot be determined how to add folders to the Explorer or how to perform further actions on the folder, as these are not shown.\\n\\n5. Tips  \\n- Monitor the progress bar for an estimated time remaining and transfer speed when moving files.\\n- Use the ‘X’ button on the progress bar window if you need to cancel an ongoing file transfer.\\n- The Visual Studio Code Explorer allows access to folders, and the welcome page provides quick actions for opening files and folders.\\n\\n6. FAQ  \\n**Q: How do I start moving files?**  \\nA: The screenshots do not show the initiation method for moving files. Only the in-progress status is visible.\\n\\n**Q: How do I add a folder to Visual Studio Code?**  \\nA: The workflow to add or open a folder is not depicted in the screenshots. It is only shown that a folder (\\\"AI USER GUIDE GENERATOR\\\") is currently available in the Explorer.\\n\\n**Q: Can I perform additional actions with files or folders in these environments?**  \\nA: Only the current status and viewing options are shown. No additional file or folder actions are visible in the screenshots.\\n\\nIf further detail is required for unshown steps or functionalities, please refer to system documentation or support resources.\",\"screenshots\":[\"Screenshot From 2026-06-30 23-03-42.png\",\"Screenshot From 2026-07-06 19-07-35.png\"],\"status\":\"success\"}"}
